  "title": "Split blunder_analysis.py (1310 lines) into focused modules",
  "description": "blunder_analysis.py mixes prompt engineering, game context formatting, LLM interaction, annotation parsing, and stats persistence in one module.\n\nSuggested extraction targets:\n\n1. **blunder_prompts.py** (~150 lines) — PER_DECISION_SYSTEM prompt, ANNOTATION_SCHEMA, _build_tool_reference, severity definitions, example annotations. Static configuration that never changes per-game.\n\n2. **blunder_context.py** (~280 lines) — _actions_by_turn (43 lines), _format_prior_context (46 lines), _format_current_turn_actions (63 lines), _game_overview, _snapshot_zone_cards, _collect_card_names, _record_field. All game context extraction and formatting for prompt construction.\n\n3. **blunder_llm.py** (~130 lines) — _call_llm (65 lines), _parse_annotation (56 lines), _compute_cost. LLM API interaction with caching, retry, and response validation.\n\nThe remaining core (~750 lines) would keep: _eval_one_decision, build_decision_prompt, eval_decisions, load_game_context, _write_annotations, _append_blunder_stats, init_api, and main.",
